    "created_at": "2026-07-16T12:59:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-07-16T12:59:58Z",
    "body": "> For the second part \"I don't see anything that ensures this is the case\" as far as I know this is just spec editors ensuring that definitions work. Provided the attributes are defined properly then this will be true.\n\nMy concern wasn't about something that spec authors could ensure:  what I'm saying is that if an author writes `<link crossorigin=unknownvalue>` in their markup and then calls the `HTMLLinkElement.crossOrigin` getter, I don't see anything that would make the value of *contentAttributeValue* at the time of \"Assert: contentAttributeValue corresponds to a state of attributeDefinition.\" be anything other than `unknownvalue`.\n\nThough I suppose, again, that I don't know exactly what \"corresponds to\" means.",
