    "created_at": "2026-07-16T13:18:51Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-07-16T13:18:51Z",
    "body": "So I can explain what happens, that crossorigin content attribute on link is defined to be a CORS settings attribute [here](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#attr-link-crossorigin). The CORS setting attribute definition is [here](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/urls-and-fetching.html#cors-settings-attribute) (ideally would be linkified as a concept within the reflection algorithms). That definition has the attributes invalid value default as the Anonymous state. So the `crossorigin=unknownvalue` 'corresponds to' the Anonymous state of attributeDefinition.\n\nThe Anonymous state has an associated keyword value so it doesn't return null, it instead returns the canonical keyword \"anonymous\".\n\nI agree that \"corresponds to\" is perhaps a bit too handwavy and should make it a bit more clear what a definition is and how a value corresponds to it including the special states.\n\n\nHaving said all that there actually is an algorithm for this (or close), it's just not linkable for some reason. See the \"To determinate the state of an attribute\" [here](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/common-microsyntaxes.html#keywords-and-enumerated-attributes).",
